@startuml
autonumber
actor "Merchant / Demo Store" as Merchant
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Merchant Service" as MerchantService
database "Redis / PostgreSQL" as Storage
participant "Parcel Service\n(Internal API)" as ParcelService
queue "RabbitMQ\n(parcel.exchange)" as RabbitMQ
participant "Webhook Dispatcher\n(Merchant Service)" as WebhookDispatcher
actor "Merchant Webhook Endpoint" as WebhookReceiver

== 1. Merchant Order Placement ==
Merchant -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/merchant/orders\nHeaders: Authorization (Bearer JWT), Idempotency-Key
Gateway -> MerchantService: Forward authenticated request (merchantId extracted)

MerchantService -> Storage: Check Idempotency Key (cached response?)
alt Key exists (Duplicate Request)
    Storage --> MerchantService: Return cached response
    MerchantService --> Merchant: 200 OK (Cached Order Details)
else First time request
    MerchantService -> Storage: Store Idempotency Key (IN_PROGRESS)
    MerchantService -> ParcelService: POST /internal/v1/parcels\nHeader: X-Internal-Token\nBody: Sender, Receiver, Package details
    ParcelService --> MerchantService: 201 Created (Tracking Number, Status: CREATED)
    
    MerchantService -> Storage: Save MerchantOrder (order_id, tracking_no, merchant_id, status)
    MerchantService -> Storage: Update Idempotency Key (SUCCESS, payload)
    MerchantService --> Merchant: 201 Created (Order Response with Tracking No)
end

== 2. Async Status Update & Webhook Dispatch ==
ParcelService -> RabbitMQ: Publish "parcel.status.changed"\n(tracking_no, status, timestamp)
RabbitMQ -> WebhookDispatcher: Consume event from "webhook.q"

WebhookDispatcher -> Storage: Fetch Webhook Endpoint for merchant_id
WebhookDispatcher -> Storage: Decrypt Webhook Secret (AES-256-GCM)
WebhookDispatcher -> WebhookDispatcher: Generate HMAC-SHA256 Signature\n(Header: X-SwiftDrop-Signature: t=..., v1=...)

WebhookDispatcher -> WebhookReceiver: POST configured webhook URL\nPayload: { event, trackingNumber, status, timestamp }\nHeader: X-SwiftDrop-Signature
alt Webhook Delivered (2xx Success)
    WebhookReceiver --> WebhookDispatcher: 200 OK
    WebhookDispatcher -> Storage: Record WebhookDelivery (SUCCESS, attempt 1)
else Webhook Failed (Timeout / 5xx Error)
    WebhookReceiver --> WebhookDispatcher: 500 / Network Error
    WebhookDispatcher -> Storage: Record WebhookDelivery (FAILED, attempt 1)
    WebhookDispatcher -> RabbitMQ: Route to "webhook.retry.q" (TTL 30s)
    
    note over RabbitMQ, WebhookDispatcher
      Retries up to 3 times with exponential backoff.
      If still failing, routed to "webhook.dlq" (Dead Letter Queue).
      Merchant can inspect delivery logs and trigger manual replay.
    end note
end
@enduml

